@flexiarg ways-of-working/inbox-zero
@title All files are committed and pushed; no mess is left in the repos
@keywords way of working, invariant, cascade live
@audience agents, operators, institution designers
@tone normative
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-11-02 by claude-16; runs correct it
@provenance declared in futon3c/holes/excursions/ways-of-working.json (claude-2 with Joe, 2026-11-02)
@why [creativity-commons/contributor-boundaries]

! conclusion: Every repo under ~/code with an upstream has no untracked or modified files and no unpushed commits.

  + IF:
    Uncommitted and unpushed work is invisible to every other participant, cannot be reviewed, and is lost on the next disk failure; a dirty tree also stops the click loop's preflight.

  + HOWEVER:
    Agents leave work uncommitted, in worktrees and on branches, because committing is not part of finishing a thought.

  + THEN:
    Every repo under ~/code with an upstream has no untracked or modified files and no unpushed commits.

  + BECAUSE:
    Uncommitted work is invisible to other participants and is lost with a disk. A dirty tree also stops the click loop.

  + VALIDATION:
    Is every repo with an upstream clean and fully pushed?
